[295.426, "\u001b[H\r\u001b[33B\u001b[38;2;188;72;72m\u273b\u001b[18G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m40\u001b[39m\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H"]
[295.554, "\u001b]0;\u2733 Claude Code\u0007"]
[295.563, "\u001b[H\u001b[2G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mrence's `/ sqrtf(head_size)` and softmax. The weighted value sum is `V[0..pos]^T @ att` with transposed sgemv.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 34 \u001b[22m- **Scalar code is copied from the reference:** rmsnorm, softmax, RoPE formula, SwiGLU, residuals and argmax (st\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mrict `>`, so the lowest index wins ties), with the same `expf/powf/cosf/sinf`.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 35 \u001b[22m- **The tokenizer is the reference's.** BPE encode is the reference algorithm, including its UTF-8 handling, byt\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22me fallback and dummy prefix. `PIECE` uses the reference `decode`: it strips the leading space after BOS and maps\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m `<0xXX>` to the raw byte. It prints the bytes up to the C string terminator, so `<0x00>` gives `HEX ` with noth\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22ming after it.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 36 \u001b[22m- **GENERATE follows the reference loop.** Prompt tokens are forced, and each command starts at pos 0. Greedy ch\r\u001b[1B\u001b["]
[295.564, "39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22moice. `stop` if the chosen token is 1, `max` once max_new tokens are printed, `context` when the position reache\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22ms seq_len. If max_new and context are reached on the same token, it reports `max`.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 37 \u001b[22m- **The KV cache is clean for every command:** before each GENERATE/FIXED/LOGITS, the rows the previous command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mwrote are zeroed.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 38 \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 39 \u001b[22m## Changes that\u001b[22Gdon't ch\u001b[31Gnge results\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 40 \u001b[22m1. **Weights copied to\u001b[29Galigned memory.** At load, the weights are copied once into a page-aligned buffer instead\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m of being read through mmap at byte offset 28. Same values, about 10% faster sgemv, no page faults on the first \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 41 \u001b[22m2. **RoPE angles computed once per forward pass.** cos/sin"]
[295.565, " are computed with the exact reference formula once pe\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mr forward instead of once per layer. They don't depend on the layer, so the values are bit-identical.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 42 \u001b[22m3. **Vocab sorted at load.** The sorted vocab for encode is built at load instead of lazily on the first ENCODE.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 43 \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 44 \u001b[22m## Limitations / notes\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 45 \u001b[22m- **Results are not bit-exact with the reference.** Accelerate's sgemv sums in a different order from the refere\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mnce's serial loop, so logits differ slightly (\u22643e-5 on the public fixtures, tolerance 5e-4). An argmax near-tie \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22mcould in principle flip on other inputs.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 46 \u001b[22m- **Accelerate threading is not controlled\u001b[49Gby the program.** It\u001b[70Gmay use multiple threads internally unless the h\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22marness\u001b[13Glimits it (e.g. via `VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS`"]
[295.565, "). Per the rules, the program does not set this.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 47 \u001b[22m- **Inputs the interface\u001b[31Gdoesn't\u001b[39Gdefine:**\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 48 \u001b[22m  - FIXED/LOGITS with more than seq_len ids process only the first seq_len.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 49 \u001b[22m  - Out-of-range ids, or an unwritable LOGITS path, answer `ERR ...`.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 50 \u001b[22m  - Unknown commands answer `ERR unknown command`.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 51 \u001b[22m  - Blank lines are ignored.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 52 \u001b[22m- **Speed:** about 65\u201372 tok/s on this machine for GENERATE with default Accelerate threading.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;175;175;175m\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m Do you want to "]
[295.566, "create \u001b[1mNOTES.md\u001b[22m?\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m\u276f\u001b[4G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m1. \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mYes\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m2. \u001b[39mYes, and switch to \u001b[1maccept edits (auto-approve file edits and common file commands)\u001b[22m for this session \u001b[1m(shift+tab)\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m3. \u001b[39mNo\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mEsc to cancel \u00b7 Tab\u001b[22Gto amend\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[36;2H"]
